{"packet_id":"D076-01","doc_id":"D076","jurisdiction":"San Diego, CA","category":"algorithmic_rent_setting","lifecycle":"pending_bill","title":"Prohibition of Anti-Competitive Automated Rent Price-Fixing Ordinance","requirement":"Would make it unlawful for a person to sell, license or otherwise provide an algorithmic device to a landlord, and for a landlord to use such a device to set rental rates or occupancy levels for residential rental property in the City.","key_value":"$1,000 per violation","coverage_conditions":"Residential rental property in the City of San Diego; applies to persons who sell, license or provide algorithmic devices and to landlords who use them.","applicability":{"conditions":[],"per_tenancy":"Turns on conduct: selling, licensing, providing or using software that uses nonpublic competitor data to advise or recommend rental rates or occupancy levels; report-publishing software using data over 90 days old and affordable-housing program software are excluded.","coverage_quotes":[]},"exemptions":"Software or products used to publish reports on rental rates or occupancy levels from aggregated historical nonpublic competitor data more than 90 days old, or from public information, and that do not recommend future rates; software used to set rates or income limits under local, state or federal affordable housing program guidelines.","penalty":"Tenant may seek injunctive relief, damages, or civil penalties of up to $1,000 per violation in a civil action against a landlord; a prevailing tenant recovers costs and reasonable attorney's fees.","effective_date":null,"valid_through":null,"citation":"San Diego Mun. Code §§98.1101–98.1104","quoted_span":"(a) It is unlawful for a person to sell, license, or otherwise provide an
algorithmic device to a landlord.
(b) It is unlawful for a landlord to use an algorithmic device to set rental rates
or occupancy levels for residential rental property.","interaction":null,"relations":[],"confidence":0.6,"conflict_flag":false,"conflict_note":null}
